# The SDK comes from GITHUB PACKAGES, not the public registry.
#
# Why the change: the package is consumed by exactly this extension, and vendoring it as a
# tarball meant a second copy that had to be refreshed by hand — forgotten twice, so the
# extension compiled against a contract the deployment no longer spoke. A version range resolved
# by npm has no copy to forget.
#
# Why the token, and why it is NOT here: GitHub Packages requires authentication even to READ a
# package the caller is entitled to. An earlier attempt committed a read:packages token to make
# the build self-contained; GitHub's secret scanning detected it and revoked it, and every
# subsequent install failed. So the token is read from the environment:
#
#   CI      NODE_AUTH_TOKEN=${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}   (needs packages: read)
#   local   NODE_AUTH_TOKEN=<a token with read:packages>
@easydev-org:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
strict-ssl=false
